SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later

Port of macos/Sources/MalachiMail/AccountWizard/AccountWizardController.swift
(the sheet and WizardRootViewController); GTK: account_wizard.blp
account_wizard (Adw.Dialog, 520×640) with wizard_toasts over wizard_nav.
An owned modal window (docs/windows-port.md §11.3: a window shows one
ContentDialog at a time, and the wizard asks "Trust This Certificate?" in
one of its own). Its title bar is the pages' header bar: Back while there
is a page to go back to, and the visible page's title; the close button
and Escape cancel the wizard. Below it the Frame of the pages, which
slide in by their order (forward from the right, back from the left),
and the toast overlay over them.
-->
<Window
    x:Class="Malachi.App.Wizard.AccountWizardWindow"
    xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
    xmlns:controls="using:Malachi.App.Controls">
    <Grid x:Name="Root" Background="{ThemeResource ApplicationPageBackgroundThemeBrush}">
        <Grid.RowDefinitions>
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
            <RowDefinition Height="*" />
        </Grid.RowDefinitions>

        <TitleBar
            x:Name="Header"
            Grid.Row="0"
            AutomationProperties.AutomationId="WizardHeader"
            BackRequested="OnBackRequested"
            IsBackButtonVisible="False"
            IsPaneToggleButtonVisible="False" />

        <Frame
            x:Name="Pages"
            Grid.Row="1"
            IsNavigationStackEnabled="False"
            IsTabStop="False" />

        <controls:ToastHost x:Name="ToastsHost" Grid.Row="1" />
    </Grid>
</Window>
